    "draft": true,
    "body": "## Why\n\nContinue Stage 7 of the storage-capabilities roadmap. The latent delta paths lacked a complete version-bound reconstruction and publication contract, and Settings advertised automatic delta transfers that were not connected to the queue.\n\nThis PR first reconciles the recent repository work, then adds a bounded native delta-download profile using existing hashing, staging and foreground HTTP bandwidth facilities. It adds no runtime dependency.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Validate block-map geometry, lengths, counts, identities and hashes at runtime; freeze source/baseline snapshots and reject contradictory or unbound plans.\n- Reconstruct native downloads privately, verify downloaded and reused blocks, reread the complete candidate and original destination, and revalidate the source before the existing local publication boundary. Empty files and shrink-only plans apply their exact final size.\n- Add explicit S3 full-revision seeding and conditional range reconstruction. Admission binds account, object, strong ETag and length, plus a private receipt from the same adapter's verified seed. Persistent JSON alone cannot authorize reuse.\n- Require exact HTTP 206/range/body metadata, reject URI aliases and unsupported profiles, and reuse the captured bandwidth context.\n- Refuse raw remote delta uploads and decline the unqualified pCloud/Nextcloud high-level mutation paths before I/O. Ordinary transfers keep their existing behavior.\n- Show a disabled, localized Delta Sync status in Settings and replace historical automatic-execution claims with the actual profile.\n\nLimits: 64 KiB–64 MiB blocks, 8 GiB files, 131,072 signatures and 32 MiB serialized maps. A new remote version, adapter restart or lost seed receipt requires fresh explicit seeding.\n\n## Reconciled source work\n\nThe initial fetch covered 5 branches, 96 PR heads and 22 tags, including Office notes/sorting, Office recovery and bandwidth PR #106. Subsequent refreshes incorporated the STL/3MF previews, content detection, pane path menus, newer Office work, main `2c373371973b2506fc4fc03e599ef093d14a4be1` and annotated `v1.3.2`.\n\nAll branch and PR heads observed at the recorded 20:54:46 UTC cutoff are ancestors. The superseded MadEdit2 alternate API remains preserved under its archive tag, consistent with its existing disposition.\n\nThe guarded Office sync pins `a379ecc455890032906098b6cf58e17504581ed0`, retaining the combined sorting/history regression and latest canonical Word fixes. Companion review: https://github.com/CrispStrobe/quds_office_suite/pull/12.\n\n## Validation\n\n| Gate | Exact source | Result |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Broad native delta/provider/queue/bandwidth/Office/mesh/staging cohort | `33198164` | 790 passed across 43 suites; 0 failed/skipped; 8,382 stable inputs |\n| Follow-up for the four newer Word runtime files | `b98cd70e` | 60 host cases passed across 6 suites; 0 failed/skipped; 8,384 stable inputs |\n| Canonical Word and editor history | `a379ecc4` | 232 passed across 19 suites; 0 failed/skipped; 2,955 stable inputs |\n| Python sync/evidence controls | Recorded input-bound receipts | 50 passed; all recorded Python inputs stable |\n| Managed Office provenance | `a379ecc4` | All 2,187 files verified |\n\nStrict scoped analysis passes. Linux validation uses Flutter 3.47.8 / Dart 3.13.7 with native hooks enabled and no dependency override. S3 coverage includes fault-injected mocks and real signed loopback HTTP ranges. Final changes after `b98cd70e` only preserve documentation and evidence.\n\n[Profile](https://github.com/CrispStrobe/CrispCloud/blob/781458d765100ae3556906ff8ca923e70c956afa/docs/storage-delta-profile.md) · [Progress and checkpoints](https://github.com/CrispStrobe/CrispCloud/blob/781458d765100ae3556906ff8ca923e70c956afa/docs/evidence/storage-delta-20261114/PROGRESS.md) · [Broad raw receipts](https://github.com/CrispStrobe/CrispCloud/blob/781458d765100ae3556906ff8ca923e70c956afa/docs/evidence/storage-delta-20261114/qualification/README.md) · [Word follow-up](https://github.com/CrispStrobe/CrispCloud/blob/781458d765100ae3556906ff8ca923e70c956afa/docs/evidence/storage-delta-20261114/office-refresh/README.md)\n\n## Remaining scope\n\nAutomatic delta queue admission, durable delta resume/path claims and remote conditional publication remain future work. This is Linux native qualification with mock/loopback transports, not live-provider, browser or mobile qualification. Cancellation is cooperative; the existing native check/rename boundary is not external-writer CAS. Ten historical Nextcloud/ownCloud live mutation scenarios remain explicitly unavailable and are not counted as passes.",
